# Attack Simulation Guide (Atomic Red Team)

This lab uses [Atomic Red Team](https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team)
to generate realistic attacker telemetry that the detection rules in
`rules/` are designed to catch. Atomic Red Team is a library of small,
scoped test cases mapped directly to MITRE ATT&CK techniques — safe to run
in an isolated lab VM.

## Setup

On the Windows test VM:

```powershell
IEX (IWR 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/redcanaryco/invoke-atomicredteam/master/install-atomicredteam.ps1' -UseBasicParsing)
Install-AtomicRedTeam -getAtomics
```

## Running the Test Cases for This Lab

**Brute force (T1110.001):**
```powershell
Invoke-AtomicTest T1110.001
```

**Encoded PowerShell (T1059.001):**
```powershell
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059.001
```

**Scheduled task persistence (T1053.005):**
```powershell
Invoke-AtomicTest T1053.005
```

## Important

- Only run these in an isolated lab VM, never on a production or
  personal-use machine.
- After each test, check your SIEM to confirm the corresponding rule in
  `rules/` fired, then document the alert in the matching file under
  `docs/`.
- Use `Invoke-AtomicTest <technique> -Cleanup` afterward to revert changes
  made by the test case where supported.

